WEBVTT

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.500
Something completely unexpected.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.850
We're just as surprised.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.990
Ocean Blue's blue miracle.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.120
What is that?

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.630
Well, just try saying it.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.130
Come on, Youichi.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.140
Something completely unexpected. Our something-something miracle.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.350
Nice.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.270
I like how standoffish that was. Just like high school kids.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.520
Sir! We have a hip commercial on our hands.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.930
You're right, Takada. It sure is hip.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:17.280
This looks very promising.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:24.540
This is our company's first departure from sports equipment, and our initial foray into developing a sports drink.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.300
A young Olympian like Youichi is the perfect spokesperson.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.790
Is something the matter, Youichi?

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.170
Sorry, it's nothing.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.050
Sir.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.800
What is it?

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:43.680
Mizuki won't close MDC if one of us qualifies for the Olympics.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.770
That was your agreement with Coach Asaki, wasn't it?

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.310
Well, you got me there.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.310
Of course, I will keep our promise.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:58.600
When you take the medal, we'll even make an original MDC swimsuit that you can hand out to everyone.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.820
Our mat for dry land training has
been torn for the last three years.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.080
We'll send over a new one right away.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.830
It just needs to be fixed.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.830
Hey.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.840
What an environmentally conscious high school student.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:19.110
You are such a unique character.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.930
I bet you're exhausted from that unfamiliar experience.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:30.440
It was the same in my own case,
but the Olympics are like a big wave.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.940
Is that dumb-sounding commercial the first wave?

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.080
I only heard the first of it this morning.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.060
To be honest, I was surprised.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.950
But it's still a chance to bring such a
minor sport to the public's attention.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:49.010
I think that cultivating young talent is much more important, though.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.020
You did well in bringing up the mat for MDC.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.970
It's been bothering me as well.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.970
Yes.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.480
<i>For MDC?</i>

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.480
<i>Again?</i>

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:23.610
The committee has reached a decision, and Teramoto and our Fujitani have been chosen for the Olympics.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:31.620
I'm sure you're all wondering why the representatives were chosen so early

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:36.130
without even conducting the Olympic trials normally held in the spring.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.550
While this early selection is unprecedented,

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:44.880
the Japan Swimming Federation's Maebara is rather fired up about medaling this year.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:50.890
So he's decided to send our Olympic representatives to the two big international meets before the Olympics.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.390
That's why the decision was pushed up.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:58.900
If he wants a medal so badly,
why are there only two representatives and not three?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.900
Having more representatives doesn't
necessarily increase the odds of medaling.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:09.750
If Japan truly has its sights set on medaling, it'd be better to trim the representatives down to only Teramoto.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:12.550
Then why was I chosen too?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.630
Because if it's only Teramoto, all expectation falls on him.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:22.420
I'm sure they decided it'd be better if he had a teammate to relieve him of that pressure.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:26.930
It will also serve as a backup in case Teramoto is off his form.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.410
So I'm just a backup, then?

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.680
Just a chaperon to be there to support Teramoto mentally?

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.690
No, I never said that.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.690
The commercial deal isn't somehow
related to the Olympic selection, is it?

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.190
Of course not. Don't be ridiculous.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:49.700
Then how do you explain the fact that this commercial was already set, when I was just selected yesterday?!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.200
They probably pushed forward some plan they had in place a while ago.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.960
Don't you think the timing is a little too convenient?!

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.200
Look, Youichi.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.460
It doesn't matter if the commercial had something to do with your selection.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:08.210
What's important is that you have the skills to be number two.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:16.980
The fact remains that you earning the ticket
to the Olympics gave everyone here a future.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:22.910
Mizuki's president said he would honor his promise of keeping MDC open.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:26.490
You all still have a chance of working hard for the next opportunity.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.510
The next Olympics are in five years.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:33.490
It's hard to imagine what'll be happening then.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.360
I don't even know what's going to be happening next year,
or tomorrow for that matter.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.130
Hey, Reiji. Wait.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.140
You won't quit diving or anything, will you?

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:47.680
Huh?

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:51.390
You won't stop coming to practice like Ryou, will you?

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:55.390
It's not really like you to bother
worrying about something like that.

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:56.280
Huh?

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:59.030
I'll be fine.

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:01.900
I was shocked, and also a little sore to hear it.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:06.900
But unlike Tomo, I feel like I've been pretty aware of my own limits.

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.980
You should stop worrying about me and focus on yourself.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:14.430
I want you to keep looking cool and plowing forward for the rest of us.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:18.890
And if you're going to worry about anyone, it should be Tomo.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:19.510
What?

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:25.630
He's been acting weird ever since he heard about the Olympic selection from Coach Asaki this morning.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:26.460
Acting weird?

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.670
He's just been really out of it.

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:32.590
Like his soul was missing.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:37.020
Even in that meeting just now,
notice how he didn't say anything?

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:49.690
Mr. Fujitani, who would you like to thank for being selected to represent Japan in the Olympics?

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.450
My mother in Heaven.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.860
I'm alive.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:57.450
You and your father both being
Olympians is something special.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.960
You don't seem too happy.

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:03.420
It's nothing.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.710
I'm happy.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.450
Thank you for the meal.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.570
<i>That's not it.</i>

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:14.790
<i>Something's off.</i>

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.720
I've got big news.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:22.920
So much has been going on that I won't be surprised unless it's something really big.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:23.480
Same.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.480
Youichi isn't here.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:26.610
No way!

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.740
Maybe he's at some meeting for the Olympics or something?

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.740
Nope, I made sure to check that with Coach Fujitani.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:36.490
Do you think he's sick?

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:43.000
Is your headache okay?

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:43.750
Yeah.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:46.320
Are you sure you don't need to go see a doctor?

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:47.880
It's just my regular migraine.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.760
If it was just a regular one, you'd still go to practice.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:55.610
<i>That's right.</i>

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:59.510
<i>I wouldn't normally miss practice because of a migraine like this.</i>

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.000
<i>I always thought I had to push through it.</i>

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.520
<i>But I don't have that drive now.</i>

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.630
<i>Do I maybe just want to skip practice?</i>

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.570
<i>Me?</i>

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.490
It's almost been a week now.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:16.860
What has?

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:19.450
Since Youichi stopped coming to practice.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.650
Oh, that.

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:32.630
Okitsu, are you disappointed you weren't picked even after you came back and everything?

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:33.640
No.

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:39.280
That woman already told me that the Olympics might not be possible for me this year.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:40.140
She did?

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:41.590
So why...

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:43.420
Did I come back, then?

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:48.900
Because diving became interesting to me.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.570
Interesting, huh?

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.520
Hey, you're looking well, aren't you?

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:14.210
I guess you <i>are</i> just skipping practice.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:19.220
Uranus' alignment means Leos are at risk of drowning this month.

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:26.040
The Olympic representatives get picked as soon as I make it back from Tsugaru, and then my rival skips out on practice.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:27.480
Can you believe my life?

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.710
I get headaches.

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.100
For a whole week?

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.120
I'm being safe.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:38.610
What's going on? This isn't like you.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:44.620
By the way, my roommate's worried that you've burnt out.

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:50.930
Tell Coach Ooshima that it's funny if he's joking,
but if he's serious, it's the stupidest thing I've heard.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:54.980
I'd get it if I won a gold medal,
but I wouldn't get burnt out for qualifying.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:56.580
You going into showbiz, then?

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:57.140
What?

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:59.300
The sports drink commercial.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.140
Like I'd ever do it, idiot.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.550
Then why aren't you showing up to practice?

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:05.080
What are you thinking?

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.640
I'm testing this because I don't know.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.670
What?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.190
I just suddenly stopped wanting to go to practice.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:15.390
I'm confused because I've never felt this way before.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:20.410
I thought I might figure something out if I actually skipped, so that's all I'm doing.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:23.140
I don't get it.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:24.660
But whatever.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:28.410
Now that I think about it,
I skipped out on a lot while I was in Tsugaru.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:30.660
But let me just say this.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:34.670
I want to compete with you and Sakai again.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.220
Even if that stage isn't the Olympics.

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:38.670
It could be Tatsumi for all I care.

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:41.810
But you need to be there.

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:49.350
What's all this?

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.410
They're from Tomo.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.040
Celebratory flowers.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.860
Can you believe him?

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.860
Congrats on the Olympics

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.860
Tomoki

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.080
This is definitely strange.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.860
He's been acting weird.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.620
<i>Youichi?</i>

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.010
I just got your orchids.

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:16.880
Thanks.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.920
<i>Sorry they're so late.</i>

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:23.630
<i>I figured the occasion called for flowers, so I talked to Hiro and we looked into it.</i>

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:28.140
<i>And those orchids seemed like the fanciest ones.</i>

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:29.470
<i>You like them?</i>

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:31.820
Yeah, they're real fancy.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:32.890
Weren't they expensive?

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:37.270
<i>Don't worry about it. My mother and father both paid half.</i>

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:39.030
So you didn't spend anything on it.

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:46.100
<i>Hey, so, why aren't you coming to practice?</i>

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:53.160
The moon's alignment means Leos shouldn't climb up to high places or do any diving this week.

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:58.440
<i>Our club doesn't work without you, Youichi.</i>

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:00.170
<i>Will you come next week?</i>

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.120
Ask the stars.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:03.000
Later.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:06.960
Yes?

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:10.130
Could we talk?

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:19.270
I'm sure you have your reasons, but I think it's time to stop.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:23.440
I can't very well overlook this anymore as your coach.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:29.790
Most importantly, you should be adjusting for your next meet.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:31.200
Next meet?

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:37.080
The Japan Swimming Federation invited Chinese divers to compete in a goodwill competition in November.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:44.470
They'll use those results to officially announce that you and Teramoto have been chosen as Olympic representatives.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:48.080
Results? The competition hasn't even happened yet.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:51.370
What if I lost to another Japanese diver besides Teramoto?

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:53.470
What'll happen to my spot?

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.340
Your spot is already set in stone.

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:58.750
Even if I make a horrible mistake in the meet?

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.230
Yes, it won't matter.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.720
That's not right!

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:06.240
In that case, they should just make their
Olympic selections at this Japan-China meet!

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:13.890
The only thing I can say to you is that Fujitani Youichi isn't the type of athlete that makes a blunder at an important meet.

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:16.000
That's who you are.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:18.740
That's not a compliment.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.300
Youichi.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:27.760
What?

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.780
You're back.

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:32.070
I only followed the stars.

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:34.520
You guys are with me.

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.520
Coach Ooshima, where is Okitsu?

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:44.270
Oh, Shibuki's out today for some electrotherapy on his back,
and then he has his ballet lesson after.

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:46.870
Ballet? What for?

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:49.280
We've incorporated it into his training.

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:54.290
I thought Shibuki would hate it, but he took it pretty well.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:58.790
Seems like they really push him,
and he's drained after his lessons.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:05.550
But I'm really looking forward to seeing what happens when you mix his dynamic style with ballet's grace at the next meet.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:09.590
You mean the Japan-China Meet in November? He's entering it?

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:10.350
Yep.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.800
But that meet...

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:15.140
I know what you're trying to say.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:19.310
Shibuki, Tomo, and even Reiji are entering fully aware of that.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:23.380
Shibuki's going to be happy when
he finds out you're back, you know.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.650
Listen up. Use those eyes of yours to find the right timing.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:36.410
Four-and-a-half?

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:43.880
You need to bring your shins in closer to your chest.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:46.250
Tighten your body into a more compact ball.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.130
Use your eyes. They're your weapon.

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:52.560
I know you can do this.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:53.640
Okay.

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:07.940
<i>The timing is off.</i>

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:10.660
<i>I can't recover from my mistakes.</i>

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:13.160
<i>Everything's off.</i>

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.520
I can't believe Youichi is making mistakes like that.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:22.600
You think he's just rusty after a week off?

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.660
It really isn't like him.

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:25.740
Hey, did you know?

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:29.930
Apparently, Okitsu is doing secret training with Coach Asaki in the sea near Chiba.

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:33.010
Training in the sea on top of doing ballet?

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.430
I wonder what he's doing.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.510
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.820
I'll have the pasta lunch, please.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.400
Iced coffee, please.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:54.040
You should order lunch too.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.770
You haven't eaten yet, right?

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:57.080
I can't.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.450
I'm a diver.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:02.310
This pasta lunch platter has 1,480 Calories.

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:08.070
Pasta has lots of calories as it is,
but this comes with bacon and a white sauce.

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:10.960
Even a pig entering hibernation wouldn't eat this much.

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:13.000
That's so like you.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.450
But I'm not sure if pigs hibernate.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:16.170
I have no idea.

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:17.970
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.160
There's something I wanted to ask you.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:24.050
Why are you working so hard?

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:24.480
Huh?

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:29.790
Wasn't your goal to get someone from MDC selected for the Olympics?

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:33.330
Well, we managed to secure a spot for the Olympics.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:38.740
So why are you having Okitsu take ballet, or teaching Tomo the four-and-a-half?

00:17:39.520 --> 00:17:42.740
Because those boys aren't about to quit.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:48.700
Because watching them keep at it even after they missed out on the Olympics,

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:53.010
I realized that a coach doesn't need a goal, she needs athletes.

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:58.760
To be honest, I don't know what will happen in five years either.

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:03.770
But I want to give it everything I've got with them now.

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:05.410
That's all.

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:09.270
I felt that way too, but...

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:12.270
Oh, are we finally going to get to the heart of it?

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:16.440
I've been in a huge slump lately.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:21.780
I thought that you might know what I should do.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:26.290
What do you think you should do?

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:28.530
I don't know.

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:30.790
This has seriously never happened before.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:34.800
I can feel myself steadily losing confidence from inside.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.500
I just started to feel that confidence doesn't only come from what you can do now.

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.800
It comes from new challenges too.

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:45.730
Tomo taking on the four-and-a-half.

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:47.860
Okitsu taking up ballet.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:50.810
Watching them, I'm the only one not doing anything new.

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:56.220
For most of your failed dives,
your chin is slack on your take-off.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:19:00.320
When you have your chin up,
it brings up your eye level as well.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:03.330
That'll send everything else off balance.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:06.690
But that's just on the surface.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:09.330
The real problem lies somewhere deeper.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:15.340
You were chosen as an Olympic representative,
but you're not happy with the way you were chosen.

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:19.380
But you have to accept it for MDC's sake.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.340
Your mind and body are at odds.

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:27.350
The reason you're sweating watching Sakai and Okitsu is because they're diving of their own free will.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:32.190
Yet you're moving along a set track arranged by someone else.

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:37.860
It's like phantom snow.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.740
Snow without substance.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:42.400
It doesn't melt when you touch it, and it's not cold either.

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:44.370
Everyone is rolling that around.

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:49.380
The snowball keeps growing somewhere that has nothing to do with me.

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:53.530
The JSF giving me a spot on the Olympics as a backup.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:57.430
Mizuki trying to use me for some crappy commercial.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:01.260
And my dad making me the key to MDC's survival.

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:03.760
It all feels wrong!

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:06.680
That's what the Olympics are.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:09.770
Yet you're trying to fight against all of that.

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:13.540
You want to put an end to this
unstoppable snowball, don't you?

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:14.270
Yes.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:17.210
Then just start making your own.

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.030
You just have to do what you want.

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:21.000
What are you saying I should do, then?

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:24.470
That's for you to decide.

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:26.280
It's your life, after all.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.800
Aren't you the one who wants to save MDC so badly?

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:32.430
So why would you tell me that?

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:33.540
Why?

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:36.030
Because you have talent.

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:38.300
I don't want to see that crushed.

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:42.300
I want to see how far you'll develop.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.060
<i>Hamburger: 250 Calories.</i>

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:52.810
<i>Chocolate banana crepe: 560 Calories.</i>

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:55.060
<i>Strawberry shortcake. Cream puff.</i>

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:58.570
<i>I've gotta get out of here.</i>

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:01.100
<i>My mind is going crazy.</i>

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:04.070
<i>I'm backed into a corner.</i>

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:07.190
Then just start making your own.

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:09.910
It's your life, after all.
